  "source_conclusion": "The complete two-file/four-hunk focus-handler fix is already incorporated in the owned legacy select: trigger click opens idempotently, both base and derived open guards precede side effects/geometry, closed close() performs no touch/notification work, and public toggle() remains available. Modern-only MDC state notification mechanics are not copied into the historical form-field lifecycle. This is a completed source disposition with mandatory artifact-required behavior evidence; it is not a local packed/native execution, G11 pass or security clearance.",
  "hunk_reviews": [
    {
      "hunk": 1,
      "file": "src/material/select/select.html",
      "change": "Trigger click toggle() -> open().",
      "candidate": "legacy-select/select.html",
      "judgment": "The owned trigger already calls open(). A focus listener can open before click; calling open again is idempotent. Explicit public toggle remains a separate operation. This changes event behavior intentionally while preserving rendered hierarchy/classes and all consumer HTML/CSS/SCSS requirements.",
      "evidence": [
        "select-focus-click-original-review.json",
        "select-focus-click-method-diagnostic.json",
        "select-focus-click-packed-admission-diagnostic.json"
      ]
    },
    {
      "hunk": 2,
      "file": "src/material/select/select.ts",
      "change": "Move _canOpen() early return before geometry/modal work.",
      "candidate": "legacy-select/internal/select-base.ts and legacy-select/select.ts",
      "judgment": "Owned base open checks destroyed/_canOpen before motion, modal or key-manager work. Derived public open checks super._canOpen before base open and trigger measurement, font-size reads, position calculation or render subscription. Disabled, empty and already-open calls avoid work; whole-method protocol reversions expose missing base/derived guards.",
      "evidence": [
        "select-focus-click-method-diagnostic.json"
      ]
    },
    {
      "hunk": 3,
      "file": "src/material/select/select.ts",
      "change": "Flatten successful-open block after early guard; avoid unconditional MDC stateChanges on no-op open.",
      "candidate": "legacy-select/internal/select-base.ts",
      "judgment": "Successful legacy opening still sets its own panel/overlay state and drives the existing historical attach/motion lifecycle. No-op focus-trigger open returns before those effects. Historical legacy open did not need the unconditional MDC form-field stateChanges notification; adding it would change the owned lifecycle without serving this fix. Both minimum current peer methods likewise guard first; their explicit attach/notification implementation remains peer-owned.",
      "evidence": [
        "select-focus-click-peer-source-review.json",
        "select-focus-click-method-diagnostic.json"
      ]
    },
    {
      "hunk": 4,
      "file": "src/material/select/select.ts",
      "change": "Emit MDC close stateChanges only when previously open.",
      "candidate": "legacy-select/internal/select-base.ts",
      "judgment": "Owned close guards !_motionDestroyed && _panelOpen before state mutation, touch, key-manager work and exit/detach. It already lacks an unconditional legacy close notification, so a closed close remains a no-op. The original16 legacy lifecycle is preserved; there is no justification to add the MDC notification. Whole-owned-method protocol and the mandatory packed case cover repeated close/touch/state/output effects.",
      "evidence": [
        "select-focus-click-method-diagnostic.json",
        "select-focus-click-packed-admission-diagnostic.json"
      ]
    }
  ],
